From: Tong <zhengtong0611@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:59:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/14] tools/mate-bots.sh: launcher for the two side-bot
 avatars

start|stop|status|place [for|against] runs the debate's side bots from
the fork's build ($PAYLOAD, default mex-builds/bots/Payload): "for" in
the lower left with its bubble on the right, "against" in the lower
right with its bubble on the left, each polling
$SERVER/face/mate/next/<persona>.

- Each instance has its own XDG_CONFIG_HOME, TMPDIR (Vulkan shader
  cache) and logs under ~/.local/state/whack-mate/<persona>/, so the two
  share no settings, prefs or caches.
- start rewrites settings.json (tutorial done, 30 FPS cap, Discord off,
  sounds 0, no random/Minecraft messages or auto-dance apps, on top, a
  built-in avatar each: default / Ayrina), speech_bridge.json (channel,
  bubble side, 30/320 px) and Unity's prefs (window geometry; a new file
  also gets the "Default" entries, without which Unity ignores it).
- Defaults: 900x820 windows at y=200, clear of the panel; both showed
  about 29 FPS at the 30 cap. XDG_SESSION_TYPE=x11 skips ME's 30 s
  "Wayland is not fully supported" notice per launch.
- PIDs in <persona>/pid, checked by executable and log argument before
  any signal; stop sends SIGTERM to both, then SIGKILL after 10 s
  (Unity sometimes hangs on SIGTERM, old and new builds alike).
- place moves running windows with _NET_MOVERESIZE_WINDOW via libX11.
