 For the cleanest demo, turn off ME's random messages, Minecraft messages and Discord presence. Set its pet, effect
 and menu volumes to 0, and keep `allowedApps` empty, so that playing audio does not trigger auto-dancing.
 
+## Side bots: two avatars at once
+
+The debate server can drive several avatars, one per channel: `GET /face/mate/next/{referee|for|against}` (the plain
+route is `referee`). An instance picks its channel with `pollPath` in its own `speech_bridge.json`; a query string
+cannot work, because the bridge appends `?after=` itself. Side-bot lines are text only: `say` + `talk on`, then
+`talk off`, which the bridge handles like a voiced line (the mouth moves and the text types at about 18 characters a
+second, then the bubble lingers for `lingerSeconds`).
+
+`tools/mate-bots.sh start|stop|status|place [for|against]` runs the two side bots from this build:
+- "for" in the lower left with its bubble on the right, "against" in the lower right with its bubble on the left;
+- each with its own `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` and `TMPDIR` under `~/.local/state/whack-mate/<persona>/`, so the instances
+  share no settings, Unity prefs or caches (Unity's prefs hold the window position and size, which the script seeds);
+- PIDs in `<persona>/pid`, stopped with SIGTERM by PID; `status` shows whether each is alive and its last bridge lines.
+
+Its header lists the settings (`SERVER`, `PAYLOAD`, window geometry, avatar, bubble size). On the i5-10310U laptop
+this was built on, the two default 900x820 windows each showed about 29 frames per second at the 30 FPS cap (about
+1 GB of memory each). Much bigger windows, or windows reaching under the desktop panel, cut every instance's frame
+rate.
